WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:00.950 --> 00:00:02.960
I wonder how long it's
gonna take the rest of them.

3
00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.500
This is boring.

4
00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:09.050
Where is it?

5
00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:12.920
Where did it go?!

6
00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:16.140
Uh, Gedatsu, your eyes
are rolled all the way

7
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:17.640
into the back of your head.

8
00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.810
Honestly, how could you expect
to see anything like that?

9
00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.210
So careless!

10
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.850
Now, how's your vision?
Can you see this?

11
00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.260
Here it is, that puny creature.

12
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:32.300
He's one of those
Blue Sea dwellers.

13
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:33.950
Is that right?

14
00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:36.280
I just thought
it was a raccoon dog.

15
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:37.520
Racoon dog?

16
00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:39.580
No. He's nothing like
a wild animal.

17
00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:40.600
He walks upright.

18
00:00:40.690 --> 00:00:42.310
That is unquestionably
a creature

19
00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:44.370
that comes from the Blue Sea.

20
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.940
Luffy!

21
00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.280
Where are you hiding?

22
00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:49.920
Come on!

23
00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:51.680
Robin!

24
00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.270
Hurry up, this is getting lame!

25
00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:57.520
Awww. Where is everybody?

26
00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:00.570
This is where
we're supposed to meet!

27
00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:01.730
Guys!

28
00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:03.150
C'mon, I'm lonely,

29
00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.110
and I'm getting a
little freaked out here!

30
00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.040
Where'd you go?

31
00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:27.120
Come out right now!

32
00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:35.570
<b>Pirate Chopper vs. Priest Gedatsu</b>

33
00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:42.160
Where are you, Straw Hat?

34
00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:44.530
I'll find you!

35
00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:47.070
I know you're still alive!

36
00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:48.400
Yeah!

37
00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:51.190
And I plan on stayin' that way!

38
00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:06.600
What the heck is goin' on here?

39
00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:15.030
What is that?

40
00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:23.580
Where could
that kid have run off to?

41
00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:28.250
Strange.

42
00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:29.420
No matter.

43
00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:31.720
I shouldn't be wasting
my energy on him anyhow.

44
00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:34.800
I have a more important battle.

45
00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:37.120
All of my strength
needs to be saved

46
00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:39.920
if I'm going to win
my fight with Eneru.

47
00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:40.960
And I'm certain,

48
00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:42.670
if I use the
reject one more time,

49
00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:47.220
my body will be reduced
to a pile of ashes.

50
00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.180
It's the end of the line, Eneru!

51
00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:12.870
What have you done?

52
00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:16.240
You... You killed our Sanji!

53
00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:18.540
It's useless.

54
00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:19.870
No pulse.

55
00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:23.130
I wish Chopper were here.
He'd know what to do.

56
00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:28.410
Hey! Sanji, Sanji. Sanji!

57
00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:30.990
It wasn't supposed
to be this way!

58
00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:32.740
Hold on, Usopp!

59
00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:34.910
Your checking his
right side for a heartbeat.

60
00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:37.620
The left side is
where his heart is!

61
00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:38.440
<b>His
Right
Side</b>

62
00:05:40.730 --> 00:05:42.310
He's alive!

63
00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:44.990
Back from the dead.

64
00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:47.080
I can't believe it.

65
00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:49.750
But he's still not well,
just look at him.

66
00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:50.920
No!

67
00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.290
You can't die again!

68
00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:54.670
I need you here!

69
00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:58.310
Hey! You!

70
00:05:58.400 --> 00:05:59.690
I don't know
what you did to him,

71
00:05:59.770 --> 00:06:02.360
but you better not try
any more monkey business!

72
00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:14.040
Damn you!

73
00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:19.140
You will stay quiet.

74
00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:21.680
Or join your friends.

75
00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:24.030
Am I being clear?

76
00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:27.620
Very good.

77
00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.200
Who is this guy?

78
00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:31.990
And how did he do that?

79
00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:33.530
What do you want, Eneru?

80
00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:37.200
What wicked reason could you
possibly have for coming aboard?

81
00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:39.540
During the six years
I've been on this island,

82
00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:42.600
I've kept your former
subordinates very busy.

83
00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:45.520
They've been slaving away
for me all these long years,

84
00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:48.190
and they've hardly
had a moment to rest.

85
00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:53.700
My Divine Warriors
have been reduced to slaves.

86
00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:56.360
They are most extraordinary.

87
00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:59.070
Truly they are of great talent.

88
00:06:59.150 --> 00:07:02.200
But it appears that their
years of hard labor are over.

89
00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:05.820
You see, this island
is no longer useful to me.

90
00:07:05.890 --> 00:07:08.270
Consequently, I no longer
require the services

91
00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:11.250
of your former Divine Warriors.

92
00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:14.630
Perhaps you suspect that I have
sinister motives in coming here,

93
00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:17.060
but I have simply come
to bid you farewell.

94
00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:19.190
That is all.

95
00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:23.450
I will say this,
sometimes I envy

96
00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:27.500
the blissfull, innocent
stupidity of Skypiea's people.

97
00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:30.170
The fools here can only see
this island as nothing more

98
00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:32.920
than a clump of
vearth in the sky.

99
00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:34.590
What are you talking about?

100
00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:36.100
Stupid old man.

101
00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:38.470
All these years you never
guessed the true reason

102
00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:40.790
we seized this island?

103
00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:43.230
The reason that the Blue Sea
flies are here meddling

104
00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:45.480
in the islands affairs.

105
00:07:45.560 --> 00:07:48.280
And the reason the Shandorians
fight so bravely to return

106
00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:51.990
to their sacred homeland?

107
00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:56.530
You see, all this is happening
for one purpose and one alone.

108
00:07:56.610 --> 00:08:00.240
There is something here
that they all seek.

109
00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:03.080
The great treasures of Shandora,

110
00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:04.670
the legendary city of gold

111
00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:07.960
that prospered on the
Blue Sea so long ago!

112
00:08:08.040 --> 00:08:11.300
Gold is what brings us all here!

113
00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:14.570
What is gold?

114
00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:17.320
And why is it
so important to you?

115
00:08:19.620 --> 00:08:22.280
Your ignorance never
ceases to amaze!

116
00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:24.660
The only people in the world
who know nothing of gold

117
00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:27.940
or it's value live in the
midst of an untold fortune!

118
00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:29.740
You didn't even know
what the goal was,

119
00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:32.110
so how could you
have won this game?

120
00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:35.940
Interstingly enough, our game of
survival is in it's final play.

121
00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:37.900
Whoever wins, gets the gold!

122
00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:43.290
Can you hear it now?

123
00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.260
The sounds of our
lively little competition?

124
00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:54.210
As a matter of fact,
I'm a contestant myself,

125
00:08:54.270 --> 00:08:57.110
so I must be off.

126
00:08:58.130 --> 00:09:00.300
Wait, Eneru.
The Divine Warriors.

127
00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:03.820
Are you going to set them free?

128
00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:05.830
God only knows.

129
00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:08.000
And he's not telling.

130
00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:10.410
Eneru, wait!

131
00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:12.690
He disappeared.

132
00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:19.990
Usopp! You're still alive!

133
00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:28.580
Make way!

134
00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:36.510
Another one?

135
00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:44.420
Hmph. These
weaklings aren't worth my time!

136
00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:52.910
What exquisite
ammunition you have there.

137
00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:57.220
Matter that dense does not
naturally exist here in the sky.

138
00:09:58.470 --> 00:10:02.640
The vearth mineral
called iron, isn't it?

139
00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:08.770
You have managed to
make quick work of my men,

140
00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:11.530
which is a difficult task
to say the least.

141
00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:13.030
My guess...

142
00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:17.950
...is that you are the great
Shandorian warrior, Genbou.

143
00:10:18.030 --> 00:10:20.790
Commander Yama, good guess!

144
00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:24.230
Now get out of my way!

145
00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:49.640
No!

146
00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:52.770
I refuse to die!

147
00:10:54.690 --> 00:10:57.610
Not like this. Not here.

148
00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:01.700
Ah! Still alive I see!

149
00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:04.160
You are tough!

150
00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:08.790
Very well, as a gesture of
respect for your warrior spirit.

151
00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:13.740
I will end your suffering
with my secret technique.

152
00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:21.050
Ten Axe Attack!

153
00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:25.330
Damn you, Yama!

154
00:11:28.650 --> 00:11:31.240
Axe Mountain!

155
00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:50.170
So very close, yet,
so very far away.

156
00:11:55.640 --> 00:11:56.970
Ha-haaa!

157
00:11:57.060 --> 00:11:59.770
Haa-ha!

158
00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:01.490
Who are you guys?

159
00:12:02.180 --> 00:12:04.220
That's a stupid question!

160
00:12:04.310 --> 00:12:06.980
– We're Deputy Divine Commanders!
– We're Deputy Divine Commanders!

161
00:12:07.070 --> 00:12:08.730
You killed our brother Satori!

162
00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:10.600
Now you're gonna pay!

163
00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:11.360
Brother?

164
00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:12.690
What do you mean?

165
00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:14.890
I haven't killed anybody.

166
00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:17.400
– Ha-haha. Ha-ha!
– Ha-haha. Ha-ha!

167
00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:21.200
Ha! You can call me Hotori!

168
00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:24.490
Ha! And you can call me Kotori!

169
00:12:24.580 --> 00:12:27.700
And you guys killed our
beloved big brother, Satori.

170
00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:29.460
Ha-ha!

171
00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:32.080
Sorry to bust your bubble,
but I don't know your bother.

172
00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:34.540
Now, you're all gonna pay!

173
00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:36.820
Pierre!

174
00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:43.640
We must deal
with these two quickly

175
00:12:43.720 --> 00:12:45.720
and return to
the business at hand.

176
00:12:45.800 --> 00:12:47.310
We need to find Eneru

177
00:12:47.390 --> 00:12:50.890
and rescue my Divine Warriors
before the unthinkable happens.

178
00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:02.340
Now, stand back, young lady!

179
00:13:02.970 --> 00:13:06.050
I may be injured, but I'd never
lose to the likes of those two!

180
00:13:06.070 --> 00:13:09.830
No. I won't stand
back this time.

181
00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:11.100
'Cause sometimes I'm the one...

182
00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:14.230
...who has to
protect my friends!

183
00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:18.690
Very well then.

184
00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:21.740
First we need to determine
which dials they possess.

185
00:13:21.820 --> 00:13:23.030
All right!

186
00:13:23.660 --> 00:13:26.450
Time to avenge our brother!
Time to avenge our brother!

187
00:13:26.990 --> 00:13:28.530
Ha-ha!

188
00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:56.730
A memorial to the city itself.

189
00:14:00.530 --> 00:14:03.200
Its descendants built it.

190
00:14:03.450 --> 00:14:05.410
After the great city fell.

191
00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:08.950
Shandora.

192
00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:11.870
That was the name
of this ancient place.

193
00:14:17.010 --> 00:14:19.130
402 S.E.

194
00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:22.470
The city, was at its
peak 11 hundred years ago.

195
00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:26.670
But then it toppled
around 800 years ago.

196
00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:31.430
That time frame
almost perfectly matches

197
00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:33.160
the hundred years
of history that vanished

198
00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:35.200
from the rest of the world.

199
00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:37.960
Perhaps this
island holds the key.

200
00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:41.170
The key to a
long-forgotten history,

201
00:14:41.690 --> 00:14:43.780
that was veiled
from the world below.

202
00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:48.030
This is a complete
map of Shandora.

203
00:14:48.230 --> 00:14:50.610
Perhaps I'll learn more
about this "Blank Century"

204
00:14:50.690 --> 00:14:53.490
if I go to the
center of the city.

205
00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:56.530
Who's there?

206
00:14:56.620 --> 00:14:59.240
Well, aren't you a
beautiful young lady?

207
00:15:07.680 --> 00:15:09.350
Where did you go?

208
00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:14.640
A concealment
technique no doubt.

209
00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:17.460
His eyes
are rolled back in his head.

210
00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:20.500
And it's really spooky!

211
00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:26.510
Gedatsu, you can't see the enemy

212
00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:28.930
with your eyes
rolled back like that!

213
00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:31.200
So careless!

214
00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:33.850
What a dimwit!

215
00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:35.980
An enemy huh?

216
00:15:36.060 --> 00:15:37.230
Oh, I get it now.

217
00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:39.920
You must be one Eneru's priests.

218
00:15:45.470 --> 00:15:46.720
Indeed, I am.

219
00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:49.430
Let me introduce myself.

220
00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:53.770
My name is Gedatsu, priest in
the service of Almighty Eneru.

221
00:15:53.850 --> 00:15:55.140
Huh?

222
00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:56.890
And I command the Upper Yard's

223
00:15:57.010 --> 00:15:59.050
Ordeal of the Swamp.

224
00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:00.100
Huh?

225
00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:02.430
C'mon, say something you jerk!

226
00:16:03.780 --> 00:16:05.200
Gedatsu, he can't hear you

227
00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:07.240
unless you start
speaking out loud!

228
00:16:07.820 --> 00:16:09.070
So careless!

229
00:16:09.080 --> 00:16:11.200
You don't normally forget that.

230
00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:12.660
Hmph!

231
00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:17.420
I advise you to watch
where you step.

232
00:16:17.500 --> 00:16:18.630
See.

233
00:16:18.710 --> 00:16:21.500
This entire area is
my territory to control!

234
00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:23.420
All around us are swamp clouds.

235
00:16:23.510 --> 00:16:25.340
And once you find
yourself trapped by one

236
00:16:25.430 --> 00:16:27.260
there is no hope of escape.

237
00:16:27.350 --> 00:16:29.930
The survival rate
here is 50 percent.

238
00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:31.730
It's almost tragic.

239
00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:34.140
Ordeal of the Swamp!

240
00:16:34.140 --> 00:16:35.180
"The swamp"?

241
00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:36.800
Best of luck.

242
00:16:37.580 --> 00:16:39.670
Hey, you're sinking!

243
00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:42.250
Fool! It has no effect on me!

244
00:16:42.340 --> 00:16:43.920
Swamp cloud.

245
00:16:45.370 --> 00:16:47.960
Milky dial!

246
00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:57.640
No way!

247
00:16:58.610 --> 00:16:59.780
He's shooting
something out his feet

248
00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:02.750
that makes him fly!

249
00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:06.260
That's so cool!

250
00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:11.620
Something's coming
out of his hands.

251
00:17:11.620 --> 00:17:13.460
One stinking,
matted raccoon dog

252
00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:16.930
is hardly worth
my precious time.

253
00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:17.930
Take this!

254
00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:21.440
Swamp cloud burger!

255
00:17:22.170 --> 00:17:24.460
A deadly swamp
with the weight of a cloud.

256
00:17:24.550 --> 00:17:27.470
Once touched,
nothing can survive!

257
00:17:27.550 --> 00:17:28.970
Wait, no, Gedatsu!

258
00:17:29.050 --> 00:17:31.760
Don't aim it at me!
Please, stop!

259
00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:38.290
He can't escape!

260
00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:41.420
I see!

261
00:17:43.430 --> 00:17:44.550
It's a cloud,
so if you try to lift it,

262
00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:47.140
your hands will just
pass right through it!

263
00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:52.950
The more you
struggle to get free,

264
00:17:53.040 --> 00:17:56.080
the deeper you're
dragged inside of it!

265
00:17:59.750 --> 00:18:00.920
I have to help him!

266
00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:03.200
There you are, raccoon dog!

267
00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:05.920
Swamp cloud burger!

268
00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:12.360
If one of those things hits me,
I'll be dead for sure!

269
00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:17.480
If you're still alive, hang on!

270
00:18:19.830 --> 00:18:20.540
Hey!

271
00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:23.860
You gotta breathe!

272
00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:25.500
Don't die!

273
00:18:29.800 --> 00:18:31.130
Oh good, you're alive.

274
00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:33.670
Thank you.

275
00:18:33.760 --> 00:18:35.880
You saved my life.

276
00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:39.390
Ha!

277
00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:41.390
Being saved by the enemy.

278
00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:42.180
Pathetic!

279
00:18:43.420 --> 00:18:45.840
How dare you, Gedatsu.

280
00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:49.010
You're gonna pay!
I'll never serve you again!

281
00:18:49.090 --> 00:18:50.380
Hmph!

282
00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:53.180
Watch, as my axe dial
drains the life from you!

283
00:18:53.260 --> 00:18:54.720
Haa!

284
00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:56.140
Yes. We'll team up.

285
00:18:56.220 --> 00:18:57.770
And together we'll defeat him.

286
00:18:57.770 --> 00:18:58.770
Very well.

287
00:18:58.850 --> 00:19:01.310
This one is called
my jet punch!

288
00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:16.000
The lethal jet dial.

289
00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:18.670
Punches accelerated with it
allow you to destroy an enemy

290
00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:22.220
before they even realize
the fight has begun.

291
00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:26.510
It's only real defect is that
it also destroys my clothes.

292
00:19:26.940 --> 00:19:29.730
This is a Priest?

293
00:19:29.770 --> 00:19:34.690
If I don't get out of here right
now, I'll end up like that guy!

294
00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:39.280
I gotta keep
my feet off the clouds!

295
00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:41.300
Those swamp trap
things are everywhere!

296
00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:42.920
If I run on top
of the ruins only,

297
00:19:43.010 --> 00:19:45.880
I can make it to the
forest and solid ground!

298
00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:55.190
Just where do you think you're
running off to, raccoon?

299
00:19:55.270 --> 00:19:57.190
Here's another jet punch.

300
00:19:58.430 --> 00:19:59.720
Rumble... jumping point!

301
00:20:04.650 --> 00:20:05.780
Rumble balls
last for three minutes.

302
00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:08.040
So, you have Zoan-type powers!

303
00:20:11.330 --> 00:20:14.210
Too bad. How about another one?!

304
00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:14.960
Oh, yeah?

305
00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:16.460
Weight point!

306
00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:20.970
Swamp cloud burger!

307
00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:22.220
That again?!

308
00:20:22.830 --> 00:20:24.330
Guard point!

309
00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:29.450
Why that insolent little...!

310
00:20:29.510 --> 00:20:30.930
Brain point!

311
00:20:33.010 --> 00:20:35.390
Rumble Scope! A weak point!

312
00:20:35.470 --> 00:20:37.100
He's got to have
some weak point!

313
00:20:37.180 --> 00:20:38.190
Anything'll do!

314
00:20:38.270 --> 00:20:40.600
I need to find
a weakness and escape!

315
00:20:40.640 --> 00:20:43.430
Jet Punch, contact!

316
00:20:52.900 --> 00:20:56.700
Even with
my guard up, it's useless.

317
00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:03.950
There!

318
00:21:04.040 --> 00:21:05.660
Look, in the clouds above!

319
00:21:05.750 --> 00:21:07.790
I can see Giant Jack!

320
00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:11.750
We're close to
the ruins of Shandora!

321
00:21:13.590 --> 00:21:15.670
Eneru's got to be up
there somewhere.

322
00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:28.640
You called?

323
00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:33.810
I'm right here behind you.

324
00:21:37.930 --> 00:21:39.680
Did you want something?

325
00:21:41.770 --> 00:21:46.150
Brave Kamakiri of Shandora.

326
00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:48.580
Eneru, you bastard!

327
00:21:48.680 --> 00:21:52.060
Have you forgotten to
whom you are speaking?

328
00:21:52.120 --> 00:21:54.210
I am God, you know.

329
00:21:55.810 --> 00:21:59.110
And I know exactly
what you're thinking, warrior.

330
00:21:59.190 --> 00:22:02.150
You're wondering
why I came down here.

331
00:22:03.280 --> 00:22:04.410
Mantra?

332
00:22:04.790 --> 00:22:06.250
I don't need my mantra

333
00:22:06.330 --> 00:22:08.840
to read what's written
all over your face!

334
00:22:09.830 --> 00:22:12.330
to read what's written
all over your face!

335
00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:17.300
But I don't blame you.

336
00:22:17.380 --> 00:22:19.340
Normally,
I don't bother to fight,

337
00:22:20.280 --> 00:22:23.360
but this time, I'm a player
in the Survival Game too.

338
00:22:23.430 --> 00:22:26.140
Besides, I'll be
leaving this land soon.

339
00:22:26.220 --> 00:22:28.560
I was just saying
good-bye to Gan Fall.

340
00:22:28.650 --> 00:22:31.440
Professional courtesy,
you understand.

341
00:22:32.100 --> 00:22:34.980
A game? A game?

342
00:22:35.070 --> 00:22:37.030
I also don't need
my mantra to tell me

343
00:22:37.130 --> 00:22:40.140
that you'd really like
to kill me right now.

344
00:22:41.560 --> 00:22:43.310
Very well.

345
00:22:43.400 --> 00:22:46.480
I must admit you've shown
great courage in reaching me,

346
00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:49.320
so I'd say you're
entitled to a reward.

347
00:22:49.340 --> 00:22:53.430
Call it a display of God's
mercy. Heh, heh.

348
00:22:53.510 --> 00:22:56.810
So, then,
I'll give you five minutes.

349
00:22:56.890 --> 00:22:59.600
For five minutes,
I won't move a muscle.

350
00:22:59.820 --> 00:23:00.900
What?

351
00:23:01.190 --> 00:23:04.110
I won't dodge your
attacks, and I won't fight back.

352
00:23:04.190 --> 00:23:04.890
Fry me.

353
00:23:04.900 --> 00:23:05.980
Skewer me.

354
00:23:06.070 --> 00:23:07.690
I am at your mercy.

355
00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:12.410
Why, you!

356
00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:15.280
But once
those five minutes are up.

357
00:23:15.370 --> 00:23:18.290
You will know what
it means to face God

358
00:23:18.370 --> 00:23:21.580
in the very depths of your soul.

359
00:23:28.800 --> 00:23:30.260
His feet.

360
00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:35.540
That's the weak spot.

361
00:23:39.250 --> 00:23:40.750
Walk point!

362
00:23:43.190 --> 00:23:45.200
Can I escape?

363
00:23:45.200 --> 00:23:47.200
I can't even see straight.

364
00:23:48.680 --> 00:23:51.060
Still think you can win?

365
00:23:54.060 --> 00:23:57.060
My legs are shaky at best.

366
00:23:57.460 --> 00:24:00.840
And the rumble ball
is about to wear off.

367
00:24:15.640 --> 00:24:17.940
All right.
It's time to stop running.

368
00:24:20.270 --> 00:24:21.860
You can beat him!

369
00:24:27.320 --> 00:24:29.360
What do you think you're doing?

370
00:24:30.680 --> 00:24:32.650
Swamp cloud burger!

371
00:24:34.610 --> 00:24:36.480
I'm always
the first to run away,

372
00:24:36.570 --> 00:24:39.190
so everyone thinks
they have to protect me.

373
00:24:40.820 --> 00:24:44.660
That's why
they can't rely on me.

374
00:24:44.800 --> 00:24:48.350
I'm going to raise
a pirate flag right here!

375
00:24:56.940 --> 00:24:58.940
Don't you know
when you've lost?

376
00:24:59.020 --> 00:25:01.360
Even the air is
my territory to control.

377
00:25:01.440 --> 00:25:02.820
You can't escape.

378
00:25:02.840 --> 00:25:04.130
C'mon.

379
00:25:14.060 --> 00:25:16.110
Oh no! He took it off.

380
00:25:16.170 --> 00:25:18.720
That raccoon dog took my shoe.

381
00:25:18.910 --> 00:25:21.790
So careless!

382
00:25:24.700 --> 00:25:28.160
I'm coming, racoon dog

383
00:25:33.120 --> 00:25:34.330
Ahhh! I'm a monster!

384
00:25:34.330 --> 00:25:36.580
I'm strong!

385
00:25:37.290 --> 00:25:40.340
The weakest
beast roars the loudest.

386
00:25:40.420 --> 00:25:42.510
One last jet punch!

387
00:25:49.850 --> 00:25:51.520
I let myself get carried away

388
00:25:51.600 --> 00:25:54.020
and nearly lost control
of my mantra.

389
00:25:54.810 --> 00:25:56.480
He only grazed me!

390
00:25:56.560 --> 00:25:58.480
That was close!

391
00:25:58.560 --> 00:26:00.020
Arm point!

392
00:26:00.460 --> 00:26:01.500
I'm alive!

393
00:26:02.340 --> 00:26:03.600
My turn.

394
00:26:04.600 --> 00:26:06.680
Cloven... Cross!

395
00:26:27.850 --> 00:26:31.860
Finally, I'm one
of the pirates, too!

396
00:26:39.070 --> 00:26:41.620
It looks like he
fell right into a swamp cloud!

397
00:26:41.700 --> 00:26:44.290
Good. Now if he
would just stay there.

398
00:26:44.370 --> 00:26:46.960
You hear me? Don't come up.

399
00:26:47.040 --> 00:26:49.630
Just keep on sinking, you jerk!

400
00:26:52.920 --> 00:26:53.720
He's moving!

401
00:26:57.640 --> 00:26:59.350
He's still alive.

402
00:26:59.610 --> 00:27:02.030
I can't believe
I lost to a raccoon dog.

403
00:27:02.110 --> 00:27:04.360
Of all the things,
I could never live down.

404
00:27:04.450 --> 00:27:06.740
And how did I get stuck
in my own swamp cloud?

405
00:27:06.820 --> 00:27:09.410
This isn't supposed
to happen to me!

406
00:27:10.990 --> 00:27:14.120
Please, oh,
please, just stay down!

407
00:27:14.210 --> 00:27:15.960
Sink! Sink!

408
00:27:16.040 --> 00:27:18.590
I can escape with a milky dial.

409
00:27:20.590 --> 00:27:23.260
Wow he really sank!

410
00:27:24.880 --> 00:27:29.380
Did I? I did. I really beat him!

411
00:27:34.260 --> 00:27:36.220
Damn you!

412
00:27:37.310 --> 00:27:38.560
No!

413
00:27:46.150 --> 00:27:47.740
You've got to stop!

414
00:27:49.050 --> 00:27:50.260
We won't stop!

415
00:27:50.820 --> 00:27:53.120
– Ha-ha-hah!
– Ha-ha-hah!

416
00:27:53.200 --> 00:27:57.160
I said stop!
They're unconscious!

417
00:27:57.250 --> 00:27:59.920
We don't care!

418
00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:02.130
These guys
killed our brother Satori!

419
00:28:02.410 --> 00:28:03.410
Killed him!

420
00:28:03.630 --> 00:28:04.840
– They must pay!
– They must pay!

421
00:28:04.900 --> 00:28:07.610
Ha-ha!

422
00:28:09.670 --> 00:28:11.380
Thanks for the charge!

423
00:28:13.670 --> 00:28:14.880
An Impact?

424
00:28:20.540 --> 00:28:22.000
Ha-ha-hah!

425
00:28:22.080 --> 00:28:24.580
I stored my farts
in a Flavor Dial!

426
00:28:24.640 --> 00:28:26.440
Ha-ha!

427
00:28:26.520 --> 00:28:27.900
So that's it.

428
00:28:28.000 --> 00:28:30.220
They have four different
types of Dials they're using,

429
00:28:30.300 --> 00:28:31.970
instead of just one.

430
00:28:33.020 --> 00:28:34.110
Ha-ha-hah! That's right!

431
00:28:34.260 --> 00:28:35.970
Axe! Flame!

432
00:28:36.100 --> 00:28:40.230
Impact! Flavor! Ha-ha-ha.

433
00:28:40.310 --> 00:28:42.230
You won't be able to keep track!

434
00:28:42.310 --> 00:28:44.770
Which one is Hotori
and which one is Kotori?

435
00:28:44.860 --> 00:28:46.900
What Dial is in which hand?

436
00:28:46.990 --> 00:28:48.530
It's so much fun to guess!

437
00:28:48.610 --> 00:28:50.450
– Surprise Dial Illusion!
– Surprise Dial Illusion!

438
00:28:50.510 --> 00:28:52.510
Ha.ha-hah!

439
00:28:52.590 --> 00:28:53.720
We know what they have.

440
00:28:53.800 --> 00:28:55.180
There's no time to waste!

441
00:28:55.260 --> 00:28:57.010
I didn't care which
one of those puffballs

442
00:28:57.100 --> 00:28:59.100
was which in the first place!

443
00:28:59.180 --> 00:29:01.140
Suck typhoon, boys!

444
00:29:02.100 --> 00:29:02.850
You missed!

445
00:29:03.420 --> 00:29:06.380
Guess which
Dial's in my right hand?

446
00:29:08.510 --> 00:29:16.360
Ha ha ha ha!
I fooled you! More farts!

447
00:29:16.450 --> 00:29:18.030
Were you expecting flames?

448
00:29:18.110 --> 00:29:20.740
Ha-ha-hah!

449
00:29:21.610 --> 00:29:22.990
He's going to ignite the gas!

450
00:29:27.920 --> 00:29:29.210
Old man!

451
00:29:29.290 --> 00:29:30.960
Ha ha ha-hah!

452
00:29:31.040 --> 00:29:34.550
Fool! He's been blown away!

453
00:29:44.180 --> 00:29:46.560
That was
a childishly obvious trick.

454
00:29:47.430 --> 00:29:50.310
I'm afraid you
underestimated me.

455
00:29:50.690 --> 00:29:53.480
Kotori!

456
00:29:55.270 --> 00:29:56.780
Return!

457
00:30:06.300 --> 00:30:08.010
Cyclone Tempo.

458
00:30:08.370 --> 00:30:10.330
You, girl.

459
00:30:11.120 --> 00:30:14.080
Retrieve my gauntlet from the
lower deck and finish him off!

460
00:30:14.160 --> 00:30:14.860
What's wrong?

461
00:30:14.870 --> 00:30:16.000
Did your wounds open?

462
00:30:16.080 --> 00:30:16.780
Forget me!

463
00:30:16.830 --> 00:30:18.370
He'll be back soon!

464
00:30:18.460 --> 00:30:19.250
Gauntlet?

465
00:30:19.330 --> 00:30:22.750
Gauntlet, gauntlet, gauntlet?

466
00:30:22.760 --> 00:30:24.640
Hey, what's a gauntlet?

467
00:30:26.220 --> 00:30:26.920
Oh.

468
00:30:26.920 --> 00:30:28.210
It's heavy!

469
00:30:28.220 --> 00:30:30.430
It's made of iron
from the Blue Sea World.

470
00:30:30.850 --> 00:30:33.100
There's an
Impact Dial inside of it.

471
00:30:33.100 --> 00:30:34.940
Use it as I instructed you.

472
00:30:35.640 --> 00:30:39.980
Yeah, I get the idea, but
I can barely lift this thing!

473
00:30:44.530 --> 00:30:46.490
Well, there's no time
to worry about that now!

474
00:30:46.850 --> 00:30:48.560
First Satori and then Kotori.

475
00:30:48.570 --> 00:30:50.610
You'll pay.

476
00:30:50.700 --> 00:30:53.110
Now it's your turn!

477
00:30:53.200 --> 00:30:54.990
He's the one who uses fire.

478
00:30:55.080 --> 00:30:58.290
He's sopping wet,
and the air is full of moisture.

479
00:30:58.400 --> 00:31:01.570
Cool Ball!

480
00:31:01.650 --> 00:31:05.030
Huh? What's this, just cold air?

481
00:31:05.130 --> 00:31:06.130
Is that all?

482
00:31:06.210 --> 00:31:08.840
Yep! Cold air, and you use fire!

483
00:31:08.920 --> 00:31:10.670
Are you mocking me?

484
00:31:10.790 --> 00:31:12.380
Do you really think
a little breeze

485
00:31:12.460 --> 00:31:14.590
can extinguish my Flame Dial?

486
00:31:14.770 --> 00:31:17.360
I'll burn you to ashes!

487
00:31:21.360 --> 00:31:24.650
That hot air
flowing over the cold air

488
00:31:24.650 --> 00:31:27.160
will cause the moisture
in the air to condense!

489
00:31:27.560 --> 00:31:29.690
It'll form a mist!

490
00:31:30.490 --> 00:31:32.540
Fog Tempo!

491
00:31:35.200 --> 00:31:36.070
What's this?

492
00:31:36.150 --> 00:31:37.590
There's fog everywhere!

493
00:31:37.960 --> 00:31:39.460
I can't see anything!

494
00:31:39.590 --> 00:31:41.380
What are you doing?

495
00:31:44.550 --> 00:31:46.720
What?
What is this? What's going on?

496
00:31:46.810 --> 00:31:48.520
I beg your pardon!

497
00:31:48.600 --> 00:31:50.430
And Impact.

498
00:31:58.820 --> 00:31:59.520
Ow!

499
00:31:59.520 --> 00:32:02.270
Argh! That thing
nearly blew my arm off!

500
00:32:05.310 --> 00:32:08.110
What do you think
you're doing, you old fool!

501
00:32:08.190 --> 00:32:10.860
The pain will pass, my dear,

502
00:32:10.940 --> 00:32:13.530
but I must say, you were superb!

503
00:32:18.240 --> 00:32:19.790
Hey, yeah!

504
00:32:19.870 --> 00:32:22.830
I protected the ship
and the crew!
